WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.780
- [Narrator] Butter
chicken is a traditional

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:04.490
North Indian dish that is creamy, rich,

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:07.530
and packed with aromatic
spices and flavor.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.370
Butter chicken, or murgh makhani,

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.800
is believed to have
originated in a restaurant

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.840
as a means to use up
leftover tandoori chicken.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.360
The tomato gravy, butter and cream

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.460
proved to be a delicious way
to soften the leftover chicken

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.150
and keep it from drying out.

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:23.360
Like all Indian dishes,
(bright music)

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.780
there are countless versions,
with nuanced variations.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.740
Today, we're gonna show
you our favorite recipe

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.923
for this popular Indian classic.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.350
One of the things that makes
butter chicken so tasty

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:38.690
is garam masala, which
is a rich blend of spices

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:41.040
that's unique to most Indian households.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.530
Now, you can use store bought,

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:44.830
but we found creating your own spice blend

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.290
makes the dish richer,
smokier and more aromatic.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.370
If you do use store-bought

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.370
just make sure to double the amount.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:52.620
Every Indian household has

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.770
their own version of garam masala.

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:58.070
For ours, we're using bay
leaves, cinnamon sticks,

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:01.720
cloves, cardamom pods,
peppercorns, cumin seeds,

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.510
coriander seeds, and nutmeg.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.970
We'll toast these spices
for about one to two minutes

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:09.270
until they're fragrant,
but definitely not burnt.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.410
Doing this brings out their aromatic oils

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.430
and intensifies their flavors.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:16.500
So please, really, don't skip this step.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.370
Once they're toasted, we'll let them cool

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:20.010
and then add them to a spice grinder

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.860
to create a fine powder.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.550
You don't have to buy a spice grinder.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:27.310
A coffee grinder dedicated
to spices works just as well.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.210
A mortar and pestle also works,

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:31.500
but that can be pretty labor intensive

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.260
and you won't get as fine a powder.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.940
Quick tip, save whatever
spices you don't use

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.870
in an airtight container
for future recipes.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.810
Next, we'll make ginger garlic paste.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:42.940
It's used in traditional Indian recipes

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:44.630
for a smooth texture.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:46.980
You can also use store-bought
for this, but again,

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.590
when testing, we found
fresh won by a long shot.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.720
For our paste, we'll use ginger root,

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.850
garlic cloves, oil and salt.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:57.690
We'll peel the ginger and blitz
all our ingredients together

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.710
until they form a smooth mixture.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:02.570
Don't forget to scrape the
sides of your mixer as you go.

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.470
Now, it's time to marinate our chicken.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.500
You can either use
chicken thighs or breasts,

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.870
but we prefer chicken thighs

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:12.140
because they are more flavorful
and less likely to dry out.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.200
We've cut them into
strips instead of cubes,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.730
because strips tend to
hold onto the sauce better,

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:19.780
but you can really do
whatever is your preference.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.950
For the actual marinade you'll combine

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.960
the ginger garlic paste,
and garam masala, turmeric,

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.410
ground cumin, ground coriander, salt,

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:30.600
fresh lemon juice, and
Kashmiri red chili powder.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.530
This is an important spice
because it gives the chicken

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:37.210
it's signature color and it's
not overwhelmingly spicy.

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:40.330
And lastly, we'll add
full fat Greek yogurt.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:43.840
We're using full fat because
more fat equals more flavor

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:47.470
so don't try to skimp out
with the non-fat variety.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:49.620
We also found that marinating with yogurt

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:52.810
is key to getting creamy, tangy chicken,

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:55.520
and it also keeps it more tender and moist

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:58.300
compared to the chicken we
made without the yogurt.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.500
We'll combine all these
ingredients in a bowl

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.380
and then add our chicken.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:03.750
Once the chicken is coated,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.280
we'll let it marinate
in the fridge overnight.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.290
That might seem like a
long time, but trust us,

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:12.220
the yogurt will start to
slowly tenderize the meat

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:13.830
and the spices and aromatics

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.760
will season the chicken throughout.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.720
But if you really can't wait that long,

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:20.110
marinate it for at least three hours.

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:21.720
Now, when it comes to
cooking your chicken,

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.670
there are a few ways to go about it.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.800
Traditionally, tandoori chicken
is grilled in a tandoor,

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.340
which is a large cylindrical
oven made of clay or metal

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:32.640
filled with hot coals or wood-fire.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.330
We found the best way to mimic

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.060
the cooked flavor of a tandoor

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:39.460
is to place the chicken on
skewers and broil for 15 minutes.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:43.030
While our chicken cooks,
let's make our gravy or sauce.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.260
In India, some people call it a gravy.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.620
some people call it a sauce,

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.710
but whatever you call it,
it's the star of the show,

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.770
and it's what makes butter
chicken, butter chicken.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:55.400
To begin, we have to choose our fat.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.450
Ghee is often used in Indian cooking.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.660
However, when we tested
butter versus ghee,

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:03.580
we found that while ghee
made the gravy richer

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.350
butter made it creamier.

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:08.390
So in a pan you'll combine
butter and oil on medium heat

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:11.930
until the butter melts,
then add in cumin seeds,

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:15.230
a cardamom pod, a bay leaf, four cloves,

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.200
green chilies and turmeric.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.830
Once you can smell all
of these wonderful spices

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:23.030
and hear them sizzle
add in a chopped onion

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:26.260
and cook for about five minutes
until it lightly browns.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.980
Then add some of that
homemade ginger garlic paste

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.330
and cook for another minute.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:34.040
Finally, add ground cumin,
Kashmiri red chili powder,

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:39.000
ground coriander, garam masala
and stir until well combined.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.580
Can you see a theme here?

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.880
We use a lot of spices in Indian cooking.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:45.090
We use them in whole and ground form

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:48.450
to layer the dish and
reinforce the flavors.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.230
Next, we'll add in the tomatoes.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.580
They add substance and
acidity to our sauce,

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:54.850
as well as cut through the
richness of the butter.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:57.210
We tested with both
canned and fresh tomatoes

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:59.820
and surprisingly we
found the canned tomatoes

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.050
were sweeter and more flavorful.

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:03.460
This can really depend on where your

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:06.670
fresh tomatoes come from,
but we preferred the canned.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:09.560
Next, we're gonna let
you in on a little secret

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:12.320
to extra creamy gravy, cashews.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:15.620
A lot of Northern Indian dishes
include nuts like cashews

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:17.620
to add richness to a sauce.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:19.450
They can definitely be omitted,

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.200
but when testing we found
they added a wonderful

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.380
sweetness and lusciousness to the dish

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.680
that just can't be replicated.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.580
So, if you don't have a
nut allergy, put them in.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:32.700
Trust us, it's going to be worth it.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.200
And finally, we'll add a pinch of salt

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:38.070
and cook for 10 to 15
minutes until the tomatoes

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:41.530
are a deep red color and
the cashews are soft.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:43.400
We mean soft.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.540
If we don't wait for
the cashews to cook down

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.470
before moving on to the next step,

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:50.770
we won't get that silky smooth sauce.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:54.140
So take your time. Don't rush this part.

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:56.670
Next we'll transfer the
spiced tomato mixture

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:58.160
into a high-speed blender.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:02.530
Add half a cup of water and
blitz until completely smooth.

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:04.350
Now that our gravy is super smooth

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:07.050
pour it back into the
pot, add more butter,

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.770
because this is butter chicken after all,

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:11.770
then sugar to balance the acidity,

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:13.490
and finally the cooked chicken.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:15.790
Cook on low with the
lid on for 10 minutes.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:18.720
This is going to allow the
flavors in the sauce to develop

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:21.400
and for everything to
come together beautifully.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:24.840
Finally, stir in heavy
cream and fenugreek.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:28.380
It's worth going the extra
mile to find dried fenugreek

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:30.290
at your local Indian market.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:34.340
It really balances the dish
and adds a nice earthiness.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:36.300
Add a little more salt here if needed.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.700
You can thank us later for how delicious

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:40.630
your kitchen is smelling.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:41.960
When it comes time to serve,

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.860
there are a variety of options to plate

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:47.080
with your butter chicken,
like rice, onion kulcha,

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:49.630
naan, roti and paratha.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:52.760
We love to serve ours over basmati rice

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:57.760
and top with fresh cilantro,
alongside some garlic naan.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:00.070
Finally, it's time to dig in.
(upbeat music)

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:03.180
And the best way to do
that is to take our naan

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:07.680
and grab the chicken to create
the perfect succulent bite.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:09.400
Butter chicken is one of those dishes

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.520
that brings people together
around the family table.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:15.860
It's a taste of home, comfort and love.

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:18.850
We hope you love it as much
as we did making it for you.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:22.087
You can find this recipe
and many more on tasty.com.

